      "writtenOn": "2023-01-20T00:30:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe there are some benefits in adding the `java_api_contribution` modules to each api domains, without `java_sdk_library` providing these internally. These modules have a sole purpose of providing the API files to the `java_api_library` modules, which are responsible for generating the from-text stubs. Adding a lightweight module is advantageous to adding complexity in an already complicated module, both in future migration (from from-source stubs to from-text stubs) perspective and the Roboleaf team\u0027s perspective (because generating a bazel rule for `java_api_contribution` should be less burdening than that for `java_sdk_library`). \n\nIf `java_sdk_library` were to create and provide these info to `java_api_library`, I believe the implementation would look like multiple `java_sdk_library` being listed as dependencies of `java_api_library`, which is basically registering from-source stubs generating modules as dependencies of a from-text stub generating module -- I am not quite sure if this is the most optimal solution.",
      "parentUuid": "72ee8169_ff5e04cb",
      "revId": "386b5e518245c43fad38424606981fc653b089f2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
